<section class="page-shell"><div class="container page-content page-content-narrow"><div class="page-hero"><span class="page-eyebrow">Renter Rights</span><h1>Know the basics before you move in.</h1><p>This page is a practical overview, not legal advice. Use it to ask better questions and document the right details.</p></div><div class="page-panel prose-panel"><h2>Key Rights</h2><ul><li>A living space that is reasonably safe and usable</li><li>Clear information about rent, deposits, utilities, and rules</li><li>Reasonable privacy and notice before non-emergency entry</li><li>A written agreement that documents the important terms</li><li>A fair process for deposit return after move-out</li></ul><h2>Key Responsibilities</h2><ul><li>Pay rent on time</li><li>Use the room responsibly and report major issues promptly</li><li>Follow the signed agreement and house rules</li><li>Give proper notice when ending a tenancy</li></ul><h2>If Something Goes Wrong</h2><p>Start by documenting the issue clearly. Save messages, take photos, and refer back to the signed contract. When direct communication fails, seek local mediation or professional legal guidance.</p></div></div></section>
